  "description": "Variation of conditions 2 (approved drawings - details of main changes outlined below), 3 (wheelchair units), 5 (Use Class C3b), 6 (residential tenure), 8 (highways works), 9 (vehicle spaces) and 18 (energy strategy) of planning permission ref. 18/4810 dated 24.06.2019 for demolition of the former day centre and redevelopment of the site to provide an apartment block rising to 5 storeys comprising 13 flats (4 x 1 bedroom and 9 x 2 bedroom), 14 houses rising to 3 storeys (10 x 3 bedroom and 4 x 4 bedroom), and one apartment block rising to 5 storeys comprising 40 studio flats with an element of care (Use Class C3(b)) with associated amenity space and landscaping, the creation of a new loop road, car parking, cycle storage and refuse storage.The main changes to the approved drawings are summarised as follows:Proposed reduction in number of flats with an element of care (Use Class C3b) from 40 to 36, and change in the layout of these units to convert them to 36 x 1-bed(2p), rather than studio flatsAlterations to footprint and height of the 5-storey block, with a 1.6m increase in height at roof level to its north-eastern corner, and increase in size of communal area at ground floor levelAlterations to detailed design and appearance of this blockIntroduction of private amenity space to all flats within this block, and minor changes to ground floor communal amenity spaceIntroduction of mobility buggy store and minor re-location to position of cycle store and refuse stores (refuse store now located externally)Changes to energy strategy",
